# Space (live server): flight by every input the client has for it, then a warp to a nav point. Elanor logs in at
# rest in Jupiter (_login_space). Each manoeuvre is a pose-mark, the input, the packet the client sends for it
# (MOVE: thrust on, off or reversed; TURN: yaw; TILT: pitch) and the pose change it made (expect-pose, on the
# camera the proxy reports: the chase camera trails the ship, so the best pose sampled during the input counts).
# - The thrust gadget (the dial at the bottom middle): its upper half is 'Forward Thrust. Click to thrust forward.
#   Click again to stop.' (its tooltip), its lower half reverse thrust, a click again stops.
# - A held (Move Forward) and Z held (Move Backward): thrust while held, the ship coasts to a stop after.
# - The arrow keys (Turn Left / Right, Tilt Up / Down): yaw and pitch while held. A keyboard sends them with
#   lParam's extended bit; without it the client reads the numpad's keys, which nothing binds (clientrun.key_lparam).
# - The right button held: the nose follows the pointer (rdrag: pressed at the middle, the pointer held left,
#   right, above, below). Left raises yaw, up raises pitch (e2e.py's pose).
# - W (Target Near Navigation) targets the nearest nav point, Jupiter Path the First, about 1.35k from where the
#   manoeuvres end: too close, the server answers Q with a MESSAGE_STRING and no warp (run 094456). The target
#   panel's >> (1248,987) steps to the next one twice, to Nav Group Shrine (54.95k, run 095049); Q (Warp) warps to
#   it: WARP, then the server's WARP_INDEX when the ship drops out, about 19 s later, some 50k on.
# Calibrated on retail 2026-11-21 (run 093925: gadget forward 1041 in 3 s, A 1425 in 3 s, Z back 566 in 4 s,
# right-button turns 133-172 degrees and pitch 70 / 78 in 2 s; run 095049 with the arrow keys and the gadget's
# reverse: arrows yaw 80 / 145 and pitch 70 / 99 degrees in 1.5 s, the gadget's reverse 743 back, the warp 49928).
# Ours (the stand-in build of 2026-11-21 06:14) passes too, and `compare` finds the SAME 201 packets (each down of
# A / Z sends a MOVE: hold VK for S posts a fixed count of downs). The shots after the turns are never comparable
# (shot_mask.txt); those at the start pose are: from the store's database state ours and retail draw space_entered
# alike (2026-11-25: 187 draws, mean 49.0 against 49.2-49.3, 2-3 cells; the 2026-11-21 49.8 / 55.9 was another state).
# Run: e2e.py --live --retail --db-snapshot 7 --instance space run sp_flight (it moves Elanor; the snapshot puts
# her back).
name: space flight: thrust gadget, A / Z, arrow keys, right-button steering, warp to a nav point
timeout: 420
include _login_space
# the thrust gadget's upper half: forward, then again: stop
pose-mark
click 640,878
expect-event antprox 'received MOVE$' within 10
alive 3
expect-pose forward 300
shot gadget_forward
click 640,878
expect-event antprox 'received MOVE$' within 10
alive 4
# the gadget's lower half: reverse, then again: stop
pose-mark
click 640,968
expect-event antprox 'received MOVE$' within 10
alive 4
expect-pose back 100
shot gadget_reverse
click 640,968
expect-event antprox 'received MOVE$' within 10
alive 4
# A held: forward; Z held: reverse
pose-mark
hold 0x41 for 3
expect-event antprox 'received MOVE$' within 5
expect-pose forward 300
alive 3
pose-mark
hold 0x5A for 4
expect-event antprox 'received MOVE$' within 5
expect-pose back 100
alive 3
# the arrow keys: turn left, right; tilt up, down
pose-mark
hold 0x25 for 1.5
expect-event antprox 'received TURN$' within 5
expect-pose left 10
pose-mark
hold 0x27 for 1.5
expect-event antprox 'received TURN$' within 5
expect-pose right 10
pose-mark
hold 0x26 for 1.5
expect-event antprox 'received TILT$' within 5
expect-pose up 10
pose-mark
hold 0x28 for 1.5
expect-event antprox 'received TILT$' within 5
expect-pose down 10
shot arrows
# the right button held: the nose follows the pointer left, right, up, down
pose-mark
rdrag 240,512 for 2
expect-event antprox 'received TURN$' within 5
expect-pose left 30
pose-mark
rdrag 1040,512 for 2
expect-event antprox 'received TURN$' within 5
expect-pose right 30
pose-mark
rdrag 640,212 for 2
expect-event antprox 'received TILT$' within 5
expect-pose up 20
pose-mark
rdrag 640,812 for 2
expect-event antprox 'received TILT$' within 5
expect-pose down 20
shot steered
# the nearest nav point as the target, then warp to it
key 0x57 until antprox 'sent SET_TARGET$' every 1.5 within 15
wait-quiet proxy 0.5 within 10
shot nav_nearest
# the target panel's >>: the next target, twice
click 1248,987 until antprox 'sent SET_TARGET$' every 1.5 within 15
wait-quiet proxy 0.5 within 10
shot nav_next1
click 1248,987 until antprox 'sent SET_TARGET$' every 1.5 within 15
wait-quiet proxy 0.5 within 10
shot nav_target
pose-mark
key 0x51
expect-event antprox 'received WARP$' within 10
# in the warp: the ship's distortion and the slipstream around it (warp_tun01a-c.w3d, pwarp01-04.w3d, sw_warp*.dds)
alive 3
shot warping_3s
alive 5
shot warping_8s
wait-event antprox 'sent WARP_INDEX$' within 90
expect-pose moved 20000
shot warped
expect-no CRASH
